## A reorderable proof
  {:label: sec-reorder}

Filler paragraph one, padding the section so the proof sits below the top.

Filler paragraph two, more vertical room above the proof for the reading band.

Filler paragraph three, still more room so scrolling can position the proof.

:proof:

  :step: {:label: stp-setup} Let $x$ be a fixed object to reason about. ::

  :step: {:label: stp-a} By :ref:stp-setup::, the first quantity is bounded. ::

  :step: {:label: stp-b} By :ref:stp-setup::, the second quantity is bounded. ::

  :step: {:label: stp-c} Combining :ref:stp-a:: and :ref:stp-b:: yields the claim. ::

::

A paragraph between the proofs so the reading band can isolate one at a time.

:proof:

  :step: {:label: stp-let} :let: $y$ be a second fixed object ::. ::

  :step: {:label: stp-uses-y} A later bound that relies on $y$ but never cites its step. ::

::

Trailing filler one, giving room to scroll the page past the proof.

